## On the phone

Tap Quick Start on Home. With an active split, today's day loads with its planned sets; otherwise you
start an empty workout. Tap the circle on a set when you've done it: it fills in what was planned and
starts your rest timer, then asks how many more you could have done (one tap, or ignore it; turn it off
in Settings › Session). Tap a set's number for its options right under it: the kind of set, how hard it
was, rest after it, a note, or delete. Tap an exercise's name for its progress, how to do it and its
settings, and the machine under the name to pick, add or fix a machine. Add exercises with +. Tap Finish at the top
when you're done; progression works out your next targets from it. To throw a workout away, use
Discard workout in the ⋯ menu next to Finish. The tour the app shows on your first
workout:

